### DEVELOPMENT PRESSURE

# compute development pressure with r.futures.devpressure module
# development pressure is a predictor based on number of neighboring cells within set search distance, weighted by distance; allows feedback for future time steps
r.futures.devpressure -n input=urban_2011 output=devpressure_1 method=gravity size=10 gamma=1 scaling_factor=1
r.futures.devpressure -n input=urban_2011 output=devpressure_0_5 method=gravity size=30 gamma=0.5 scaling_factor=0.1
# higher gamma means more rapid decrease of development influence with distance; size is hald the size of the moving window
# lower gamma means that local development influences more distant places
# two layers with different gamma and size parameters are derived for the potential statistical model




